MID_SE_Led_Sci_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_001: Well, hello. I must tell you I feel as though a fiery\nwind has struck my heart, so great is your beauty.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_002: Oh my, you are very pretty too!
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_003: We are a perfect pair then, no? Come, let us explore\neach other's most beautiful attributes in more detail.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_004: Sirocco, if you have time to seduce innocent women,\nyou have time to work.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_005: Wait, is this your girlfriend? I...I didn't mean to...\nI wasn't trying to...
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_006: Hmhmhm. You can be quite endearing, Miss Leda.\nEspecially when you're jealous.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_007: But you've nothing to worry about. No matter whose\nbed I'm warming, it is you who owns my heart.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_008: You're ridiculous. I saved a cute girl from the\nclutches of a would-be pretty boy. That is all.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_009: "Would-be pretty boy"? I'm certain you're the only\nwoman who'd rate this face so poorly.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_010: Besides, there's no need to be petulant. Not when\nI'm so very ready and willing to be with you.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_011: Please, I've made no such request. My advice—stop\nwasting your time on pointless pursuits.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_012: You are surprisingly stubborn. I never thought you'd\nremain so very unmoved by my overtures.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_013: You thought I'd swoon the moment you slathered on\nthe charm? I can't be the only woman to reject you.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_014: In fact, I've seen the goddess Kalla herself swat away\nyour silly advances.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_015: My lady is a special case.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_016: I have no doubt my words of love and adoration are\nbut a passing breeze to her.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_017: A passing breeze? Ha! I'd say your words are more\nlike a noisy bird's incessant chirping.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_018: Hahaha. I should've known that you and the goddess\nof my heart would see me in the same light.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_019: Is that right? Two women find your flirtations\nlaughable. Yes, it must be terribly shocking for you.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_020: Let me explain it plainly. I will never accept an\ninvitation from you. Remember that.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_C_021: Ah, so cold. But that makes it all the more exciting.\nOne day, Miss Leda, I will set your heart ablaze.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_001: Miss Leda, might today be the day you join me for\ncoffee? Surely we could brew up something delicious.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_002: You can ask as often as you like, but my answer will\nremain the same. No. Gods, but you are persistent.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_003: I am, it's true. However, I have to admit I rarely\npursue anyone for as long as I have you.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_004: When one lady declines, I simply set my sights on\nthe next. Clinging to you like this is terribly tactless.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_005: And yet, for some reason, I can't let you go.\nHmm, could it be? Is it possible...that I have...
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_006: Your words drip with honey. However, I am not a\nbee, and I will never feel what you want me to feel.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_007: That's unfortunate. I think I might actually be\nquite serious.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_008: Besides, I'm just a stand-in as far as you're\nconcerned. It's Kalla's love you really want.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_009: I'm sorry. Do you truly believe I wish to be partnered\nwith my lady?
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_010: I do not. Though she is the goddess of my heart,\nmy feelings for her are far more pure and noble.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_011: That's hard to believe. But I do believe this: I am of\nHouse Cohendia. Kalla's blood flows through me.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_012: I even look a bit like her, don't I? You can't have her,\nso you've settled on the next best thing...me.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_013: Even if that were true, please understand that I was\nan orphan when the wind carried me to her temple.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_014: My lady took me in, cared for me, and loved me as if\nI were her own son.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_015: She and I are bound by the love of mother and child.\nIt is not the bond shared by lovers.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_016: And so... Hm. We will never have that kind\nof relationship.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_017: I understand. I went too far, and I'm sorry for\nwhat I said...
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_018: You have nothing to apologize for, Miss Leda.\nJust knowing you understand me—
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_019: But I'm not interested in someone who has nothing\nbut good looks and bad pickup lines to offer.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_020: I demand you do better and be better than the many\npathetic and awful men out there, Sirocco.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_021: And while it's an honor to be compared to Kalla,\nI refuse to be anyone's stand-in.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_022: I also refuse to look at that dejected face. So, please,\nstop being so glum. It doesn't suit you.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_023: Ah!
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_024: Perhaps I do prefer that sly grin of yours. Go on, try\nto seduce me with one of your idiotic lines.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_025: Hahaha. Just when you've given me the coldest\nshoulder, you begin warming to my advances?
MID_SE_Led_Sci_B_026: You truly are a mystery to me, Miss Leda.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_001: It's so striking, that night sky. Perhaps we could sing\neach other to sleep—a rare comfort in this dark time.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_002: Such tranquil moments are vanishingly sparse now.\nWould you not agree, Leilidahna?
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_003: I'd prefer it if my father were the only man to call\nme by that name.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_004: Of course... That was impolite of me.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_005: It may be presumptuous to offer this olive branch,\nbut I don't mind if you want to call me Syracusio.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_006: Yeah, sure, OK. I'm sorry—does that name have a\nspecial meaning for you?
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_007: Sirocco is a pseudonym I gave myself. Syracusio is\nthe name my lady Kalla gave to me.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_008: The only things that truly matter to me are what I\nowe to my lady...
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_009: My body and my life and my name. "Syracusio,"\nwhich Kalla assigned me.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_010: Holler out those syllables, and I will ride to you on\nthe wind, no matter the time nor the place you're in.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_011: I see. So this is your way of showing me how\nsincere you are?
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_012: Yes, it is. Not because you're from House Cohendia,\nbut because you're you, Miss Leda.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_013: I know.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_014: We've been together for a long time. I can tell when\nyou're being serious.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_015: Fine, then. Tell me...do you finally understand how\nI feel about you?
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_016: Heh. I can tell that stern expression doesn't\nmuch suit you.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_017: Honestly, Miss Leda, you defy my expectations at\nevery turn.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_018: But perhaps that's why I've always been drawn\nto you.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_019: So, you really do enjoy the way I torment you?\nYou poor, poor thing.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_020: I have your sympathy at last. Have mercy on me,\nthen. Call me by my true name—call me Syracusio.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_021: You never give up, do you? No, I don't think I'll\ncall you by that name right now.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_022: If I'm ever ready to let you wrap your arms around\nme and call me Leilidahna...
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_023: That's when I'll call you by your real name.\nCan you wait until then, Sirocco?
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_024: Of course I can. I have grown accustomed to waiting\nfor you, Miss Leda.
MID_SE_Led_Sci_A_025: I will wait for you forever.